From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: stale backing fix, sub 102 unmaps every GPU range into destroyed memory and releases its device range (EDEN_UP_STALE_BACKING_FIX)

DRAFT, not built. Port of zortos293/Lichii #1199 and the release half of #1236 (PantACRO4life's
backing-lifetime fixes, 99ivs's release-on-destroy diagnosis), as carried in Frizti/Fritchii v5.7
45e164c and 506a5ca; read through the GitHub API only. Our 0039 (EDEN_NX2_REFRESH_DEVICE_RANGES)
already carries the refresh half of #1236 and stays as it is.
EDEN_UP_STALE_BACKING_FIX=1 (boot, exact 1): sub 102 drops GPU-only tiles of the memory, unmaps
every recorded GPU range into it (the own one and any 211 range), maps the region's own memory
back under GPU-only ranges, and releases the memory's device (SMMU) range; a heap-mapper map that
overlaps a heap release still queued for the GPU thread is itself queued behind it.
EDEN_UP_STALE_BACKING_FIX_VERIFY=1 (boot, exact 1): with the fix off, count only (the old Unmap
runs as before, outside the region lock; the counting takes the region lock for a short read-only
walk); with the fix on, check after each 102 that no recorded GPU range still reaches the memory.
With either switch every heap map also counts heap pages whose device page is not the CPU page
(the 0039 comparison, count only), in the queued heap-map job too. Counter line
"EDEN_UP_STALE_BACKING_FIX <check|fix> counts:" at the first 102, then at most every 10 s from a
102 or from a map; per-range warning for the first 32, then every 1000th.
Off: one branch on two static bools per 102, per heap map and per heap release, one thread_local
bool test per device-range release; no lock, list, log or page walk.

Known limits, documented and not fixed:
- Heap pages still held by another heap entry (a 211 sub-range of the destroyed memory, or a
  second address space of the session) keep their old backing after the fix: the queued heap
  unmap only lowers their count. _VERIFY shows them as "pages stale at map"; nothing repairs them.
- "maps overlapped a queued release" is no park signal in count mode: in count mode 102 releases
  nothing, so the count only sees the older release callers (decoder images) and is near 0 by
  construction. Decide on "other GPU ranges" and "pages stale at map".
- Tiles in sparse regions (216 through MapSparseTile) are not touched (upstream the same).

Reviewed draft v2 (third review, "builds as a count-only arm"), corrections applied here: the
counter line also prints from the map path (counters moved to shared atomics,
Nx2StaleBackingStats); "released" is counted inside Nx2Release when it really frees a device range
for a 102 (exact key, last reference; check mode keeps "would release" by exact start); the
after-check of the own device range that could never fail is dropped; stale pages are also
counted inside the queued heap-map job; count-mode wording "may keep old pages".
